    "chunk_text": "w;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2451$24 - 2025 wf.daia;= ui 27 jeks nodod - 2025.08'27No. 2451/24 - WEDNESDAY, AUGUST 27, 2025\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\n1A - G 45256 - 05 (08/2025) This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nREGULATIONS MADE BY THE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS UNDER SECTIONS 32 AND 33 OF SPORTS LAW No. 25 OF 1973 AS AMENDED.\n\nI, Sunil Kumara Gamage, Minister of Youth Affairs and Sports, in terms of the powers vested in me under Sections 32 and 33 of the Sports Law No. 25 of 1973, as amended, do hereby direct as follows;\n\n1. I temporarily suspend the registration of Karate Do by virtue of the powers vested in me under Section 32 and 33 of the Sports Law No. 25 of 1973 and its amendments.\n\n2. By virtue of the powers vested in me under Section 33 of the Sports Law No. 25 of 1973, as amended, I hereby appoint a Working Task Force consisting of the following members for the limited purpose of adopting the new Constitution of Karate Do, registering new eligible members of Karate Do, and conducting the Special General Meeting (SGM) and the Annual General Meeting (AGM) in accordance with the provisions of the said new Constitution.\n\n1. Mr. M. H. Marso, Deputy Inspector General of Police (Retired)\u2013 Chairman\n\n2. Mr. Niluka Karunaratne, Representative of National Olympic Committee\n\n3. Mr. R. M. L. N. Bandara, Senior Superintendent of Police (Rtd.)\n\n4. Mr. P. Upul Abewickrama\n\n5. Mr. M. H. Ananda Kumara, Attorney at Law\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'08'27Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 27.08.20252A"
