    "chunk_text": "WHEREAS, the Government has recognized the necessity of implementing a strategic program in an accurate and expeditious manner to promote the growth of the tourism industry, which has the potential to generate foreign exchange efficiently and expeditiously,\n\n1. Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism\n\n2. Hon. Deputy Minister of Tourism\n\n3. Secretary to the President\n\n4. Secretary, Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development\n\n5. Secretary, Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government\n\n6. Secretary, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism\n\n7. Secretary, Ministry of Environment\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'08'20Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 20.08.2025\n\n3A\n\n8. Secretary, Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation\n\n9. Secretary, Ministry of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation\n\n10. Additional Secretary (Development), Tourism Division, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism\n\n11. Chairman, Urban Development Authority\n\n12. Chairman, Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau\n\n13. Chairman, Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management, Sri Lanka Convention Bureau\n\n14. Director General, Central Cultural Fund\n\n15. Director General, Department of Coastal Conservation\n\n16. Director General, Department of Irrigation\n\n17. Director General, Department of Wildlife\n\n18. Director General, Department of Forest Conservation\n\n19. Director General, Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority\n\n20. Controller General, Department of Immigration and Emigration\n\n21. Director General, Mahaweli Development Authority\n\n22. Inspector General of Police, Police Department\n\n23. Duminda Hulangamuwa Esquire\n\n24. Krishan Balendra Esquire\