    "chunk_text": "x. Provide strategic guidance to the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management with regard to training and development of human resources.\n\nxi. Promote the innovative tourism product development with the aim of supporting inclusive and long-term economic growth and enhancing overall societal well-being.\n\nxiii. Develop the appropriate systems and develop a regulatory framework for licensing commercial digital platforms and applications in the tourism industry and ensure that operations are carried out in accordance with standards.\n\nxiv. Intervene in any matter deemed necessary by the Committee for the development and advancement of the tourism sector.\n\n3. Monitoring and Evaluation\n\ni. Ensure that all institutions in the tourism sector, including the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau, the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management, and the Sri Lanka Convention Bureau, are committed to implementing the core activities outlined in their annual action plans, which are aligned with their respective long-term strategic plans, and provide assistance and monitor in further strengthening of the intergovernmental mechanism aimed at achieving the intended objectives relating to tourism development, regulation, branding, and human resource development.\n\nii. Monitor the implementation of awareness programmes and mobile services conducted for tourism service providers pertaining to hospitality services and resort registration.\n\n4. Extension to the Local Level\n\ni. Establish specific committees at the district and divisional levels with specific members, specific terms of reference and time frame. Ensure representation from both the public and private sectors for these committees.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'08'20Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 20.08