    "chunk_text": "7.2 During the Perahara season Government Covid 19 Health Advice should be thoronghly established boutiques which are currently selling Flowers and Trade On Either side of the road Kotaambe to Kataliyanpalla other sacred items in the camp area.\n\n7.4 Hawkers are not allowed to sell anything within the camp area after 7.00 p.m.\n\n7.5 Each of the building and stall be pieced with a garbage containers and garbage shall be disposed in such containers.\n\n7.6 All processed foods exposed for sale shall be kept in boxes with covers so as to protect them from \ufb02ies.\n\n8. Environment -\n\n8.1 No person shall bring or throw away plastic bottles, shopping bags, lunch sheets etc in the camp area.\n\n8.2 Plastic wastes which are brought in to the camp area shall be dumped only into relevant garbage containers.\n\n8.3 Thorough attention shall be paid to make the camp area a plastic free area.\n\n9. Beggars -\n\n\u2022 No person shall beg or solicit arms within the camp area except such places as may be appointed for the purpose outside the sacred area.\n\nK. G. S. NISANTHA, District Secretary/Government Agent, Of\ufb01cer in Charge of the Esala Festival Camp, At the Sabaragamuwa Maha Saman Devalaya.\n\nAt the District Secretariat Rathnapura, On 11th August 2025.\n\nEOG 08 - 0114"
